🔐 User & Permission Management

10. chmod & chown
chmod 755 file     # rwxr-xr-x
chown user:group file

11. Soft link vs Hard link
Soft link: Pointer to original file path; breaks if source is deleted.
Hard link: Pointer to the same inode; survives even if original is deleted.

12. Give sudo access

Edit /etc/sudoers using visudo and add:
username ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL

Services & Process Management

13. cron vs at
cron: Repeats jobs (e.g., daily).
at: One-time scheduled job.

14. Kill a process
ps aux | grep processname
kill -9 PID

15. Service fails to start
Check status: systemctl status servicename
Logs: journalctl -xe or check /var/log/messages

Networking & Ports

16. Check open ports
netstat -tuln       # Deprecated but common
ss -tuln            # Faster & modern
lsof -i :80         # To check who is using port 80

17. Check if a port is listening
ss -ltn | grep 22    # e.g., SSH
18. Network tools
ping, traceroute, ifconfig (deprecated), ip a (preferred)
Logs & Security

19. Where are auth logs stored?

/var/log/secure   # RHEL/CentOS
/var/log/auth.log # Ubuntu/Debian
20. What is SELinux?

Security layer for process access control.

Modes:

Enforcing: Blocks unauthorized access.

Permissive: Logs violations but doesn’t block.

